{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=========================================================================\nCORRECTION to the handoff block: the 'empty assignee' is NOT a claim bug.\n=========================================================================\n\nMy earlier handoff note said 'rebar claim --assignee reported success but stored an EMPTY\nassignee — worth checking after any future claim', implying a defect in claim. THAT WAS WRONG.\nInvestigated properly at the operator's prompting; claim is correct.\n\nWHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS (proven, not inferred):\n * The CLAIM event wrote the value correctly: commit 494efd886 'ticket: CLAIM acb2' contains\n   EDIT.json -> \"data\":{\"fields\":{\"assignee\":\"RebarBotNava\"}}. Every later assignee-bearing\n   EDIT also wrote \"RebarBotNava\". NO event ever wrote ''.\n * The '' comes from a LATER RECONCILER-AUTHORED EDIT. RebarBotNava is a BARE HANDLE; the\n   reconciler cannot resolve it to a Jira user, treats the ticket as unassigned, and the\n   inbound differ writes assignee='' back over the local value.\n * This is the documented failure mode of CLOSED bug 544e, reproduced live in session log\n   bb27 ('claim wrote EDIT {assignee:\"joe\"}; ~143s later a reconciler-authored EDIT wrote\n   {assignee:\"\"}'; validate_assignee_exists(\"joe\") REJECTED as ambiguous,\n   \"joeoakhart@navapbc.com\" RESOLVED to an accountId).\n * CONTROL that killed my wrong hypotheses: throwaway probe tickets (NOT Jira-bound) retained\n   'RebarBotNava' indefinitely. So it is not arg parsing (space-separated --assignee works\n   fine), not the parent-first cascade (also sets it fine), and not the close.\n\nROOT CAUSE IS DOCUMENTATION, per the operator's framing: AGENTS.md:75, :106 and the library\nexample at :238 all instruct 'claim <id> --assignee <you>' / assignee=\"me\" — an unconditional\noverride of ticket.default_assignee, which rebar.toml:66 sets to the Jira-RESOLVABLE\njoeoakhart@navapbc.com. claim.py:124-125 applies the default ONLY when assignee is None, so\nfollowing AGENTS.md guarantees the default is never reached AND that a bare handle is used.\ndocs/config.md:397-400 documents the resolvability requirement CORRECTLY, so the two docs\ncontradict and the one agents load at launch is the wrong one.\n\nFILED: bug 5cc0-1005-018e-4085 (bilingual-raptorial-furseal), priority 2, linked\ndiscovered_from acb2 and relates_to 544e + c36c, file_impact on AGENTS.md + docs/config.md.\nFix is documentation (plus an optional bare-handle warning at claim time); claim's\nexplicit-wins precedence is correct and needs no change.\n\nREMEDIATED THE ACTUAL TICKETS: epic e369 and story acb2 now carry\nassignee='joeoakhart@navapbc.com' (Jira-resolvable, survives reconcile).\n\nFOR THE NEXT SESSION: claim with plain 'rebar claim <id>' (NO --assignee) so the configured\ndefault applies. If you must be explicit, pass joeoakhart@navapbc.com, never a bare handle.\n\nCLEANUP: three throwaway probe tickets were created during this investigation and are titled\n'ABANDONED probe ticket (arg-parsing investigation) — do not work', each with a comment saying\nso: 8890-a360-e99d-4471 (task), 1c32-57e7-d8ff-4a0a (story), 1f60-ec23-365a-44d6 (epic).\nThey are in_progress and carry no real work. Close or delete them at will.\n========================================================================="},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785339431654530001,"uuid":"1e9e0100-999a-433d-b727-12527fd4519c"}